      "body": "## Motivation\n\nHF3FS metadata allocation raises `KeyError` when a batch consumes all free pages and there are no confirmed pages to evict. Allocations made earlier in that request are lost to the caller. For example, reserving three keys in a two-page namespace returns HTTP 500 and leaves that namespace with no usable pages. Overlapping unconfirmed write batches can also reach this state.\n\n## Modifications\n\nReturn `(False, -1)` for keys that cannot be allocated, preserving the successful reservations in the response. Both existing HF3FS write paths already skip this sentinel and return `False` for that key, so callers can confirm successful writes or release failed writes normally. Add CPU tests for capacity exhaustion, overlapping reservations, recovery, existing-key/LRU behavior, and the HTTP response.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- New tests: **5 failed / 1 passed before; 6 passed after**.\n- Exercised both actual backend write methods with the project's file-backed `Hf3fsMockClient`: a three-key batch in two pages returns `[True, True, False]`, successful pages read back correctly, and the refused key can be retried.\n- Local CPU harnesses load unchanged metadata classes and backend methods from source while excluding unrelated GPU/native import initializers. Native 3FS and GPU inference were not run.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo inference performance claim; this changes the exhausted-capacity error path.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Added registered CPU tests.\n- [x] Touched-file pre-commit hooks, including CPU test registration.\n- [x] Preserved the existing client protocol and LRU allocation behavior.\n\nAI assistance was used for implementation, regression tests, and review.\n\n## Combined review validation, October 13\n\nApplied #42059, #42081 and #42082 together to main `684fea8af3b11a5b51ec9966c02959a32ad3421c` in an isolated checkout. All three patches apply cleanly. The combined capacity, snapshot and shutdown suites pass: 13 test methods and 3 subtests. Running the same tests against main without the fixes reproduces the capacity, snapshot and shutdown failures.\n\nThis CPU harness executes the repository metadata classes and tests with real FastAPI, threading and JSON persistence, while excluding unrelated GPU and native backend import initialization. This is combined source validation, not native HF3FS or GPU coverage. The latest base CI gate stops before these tests because the required `run-ci` label is missing.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36862763905](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36862763905)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36862763346](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36862763346)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36862763879](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36862763879)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
